<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/icon.png" />
    <title>API Credits</title>
    <style>
      body {
        background: #000;
        color: #f1f1f1;
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        max-width: 960px;
        margin: auto;
        padding: 40px;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      h1,
      h2 {
        color: #ffcc00;
      }

      a {
        color: #66ccff;
      }

      img {
        max-width: 150px;
        display: block;
        margin: 10px 0;
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <h1>Credits</h1>
    <p>Anikawa would not be possible without these platforms and APIs:</p>

    <h2>TMDB</h2>
    <a
      href="https://www.themoviedb.org"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      <img
        src="/tmdb-full.svg"
        alt="TMDB Logo"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      Visit TMDB
    </a>
    <p>Used for anime and episode metadata, descriptions, and images.</p>
    <p>
      This website uses TMDB and the TMDB APIs but is not endorsed, certified,
      or otherwise approved by TMDB.
    </p>

    <h2>YouTube</h2>
    <p>
      Video content is embedded from AniOneAsia’s official YouTube channel using
      the YouTube Data API. Only publicly embeddable videos are displayed.
    </p>

    <footer>
      API data is used in compliance with each platform’s attribution
      requirements.
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
